### Food Delivery Platform - Notification Service
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (named requests pass ids between calls).
### Prerequisite: run user-service.http ... payment-service.http first: their events (sign-ups, restaurant
### reviews, orders, payments, refunds) are what this service turns into notifications.
###
### Emails: open Mailpit at http://localhost:8025 to read every email the platform sent.
### SMS and push are simulated: see the notification-service log ("SMS sent (simulated)", "Push sent").

@gateway = http://localhost:8080

@customerEmail = meera.iyer@example.com
@customerPassword = Meera1234
@ownerEmail = arjun.spicehub@example.com
@ownerPassword = Owner1234
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123

@customerId = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.userId}}
# Every call carries the access token of a sign-in above (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that).
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@ownerToken = {{ownerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@notificationId = {{inbox.response.body.$.content[0].id}}
@failedId = {{failed.response.body.$.content[0].id}}


### ============================ SETUP ============================

### 1. Logins -> customerId, ownerToken, adminToken
# @name customerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{customerEmail}}", "password": "{{customerPassword}}" }

###
# @name ownerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{ownerEmail}}", "password": "{{ownerPassword}}" }

###
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### ======================= MY INBOX (any role) =======================

### 2. The customer's in-app notifications, newest first (order placed, accepted, refund ...)
# @name inbox
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 3. Only the unread ones
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/notifications?unreadOnly=true
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 4. The badge on the bell
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 5. Read the newest one (reading it again keeps the first read time)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/notifications/{{notificationId}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 6. Somebody else's notification: 404
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/notifications/{{notificationId}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 7. Mark everything as read
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 8. The restaurant owner's inbox: "New order #..." and cancelled orders
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### ======================= ADMIN: MONITORING =======================

### 9. Everything about one customer (all channels), newest first
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/notifications?recipientUserId={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 10. Emails only
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/notifications?channel=EMAIL&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 11. Skipped ones (e.g. text messages for users without a phone number)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/notifications?status=SKIPPED
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 12. Failed ones (gave up after 5 attempts) -> failedId
# @name failed
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/notifications?status=FAILED
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 13. Today's totals per status and channel
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/notifications/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 14. One notification with its delivery details: attempts, last error, address used
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/notifications/{{notificationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ======================= ADMIN: RESEND =======================
### To produce a FAILED notification: docker compose stop user-service, place or cancel an order,
### wait about 20 minutes (5 attempts: 10s, 1m, 5m, 15m), then docker compose start user-service.

### 15. Send a FAILED (or SKIPPED) notification again (audited)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/notifications/{{failedId}}/resend
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "user-service was down during the delivery attempts" }

### 16. A SENT notification cannot be resent: 409
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/notifications/{{notificationId}}/resend
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Try" }

### 17. Audit history of the resent notification
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/notifications/{{failedId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 18. Customers cannot see these screens: 403
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ======================= EVENTS (Kafka, Phase 9) =======================
### Consumed: UserRegistered, RestaurantChanged, OrderStatusChanged, OrderCancelled, PaymentStatusChanged
### (consumer group notification-service; each event is applied once, see processed_events).
### Consumer lag and dead-letter topics: Kafka UI http://localhost:8090

### OrderStatusChanged schema (new in Phase 9, published by order-service)
GET http://localhost:8091/subjects/fooddelivery.order.status-changed-value/versions/latest

### Mailpit API: the latest emails
GET http://localhost:8025/api/v1/messages?limit=10


### ========================= OPERATIONS =========================

### Health (direct)
GET http://localhost:8086/actuator/health

### Swagger UI: http://localhost:8086/swagger-ui.html
GET http://localhost:8086/v3/api-docs
